(6637300, 989744, 49018, '<td valign="top">Funny and very expressive. The choice of hue works very well in framing her. 8</td>', 'Funny and very expressive. The choice of hue works very well in framing her. 8', '2012-01-06 21:37:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(6637303, 990773, 49018, '<td valign="top">Mysterious and cyberpunk. Excellent lighting. 9</td>', 'Mysterious and cyberpunk. Excellent lighting. 9', '2012-01-06 21:39:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(6637304, 990311, 49018, '<td valign="top">Very nice expression and frank image. 7</td>', 'Very nice expression and frank image. 7', '2012-01-06 21:40:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(6637305, 990020, 49018, '<td valign="top">I love her expression and smile. I find the image a bit overprocessed.</td>', 'I love her expression and smile. I find the image a bit overprocessed.', '2012-01-06 21:40:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(6637310, 990721, 49018, '<td valign="top">The Baskerville''s hounds are again on the loose, with the good light? Very effective lighting, as always. I perhaps like it even better with the texture layer you added in the other version, as it makes for a more unusual, more unexpected look.</td>', 'The Baskerville''s hounds are again on the loose, with the good light? Very effective lighting, as always. I perhaps like it even better with the texture layer you added in the other version, as it makes for a more unusual, more unexpected look.', '2012-01-06 21:47:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6637311, 990794, 49018, '<td valign="top">Nice low-key.</td>', 'Nice low-key.', '2012-01-06 21:47:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(6637318, 990356, 49018, '<td valign="top">Very SF from the 60''s :)</td>', 'Very SF from the 60''s :)', '2012-01-06 21:49:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(6637321, 990744, 49018, '<td valign="top">A very good idea and in a sense a statement about postprocessing in portrait :) I think I would have liked it even better if the light would mimic the duality on her body as it does on her face.</td>', 'A very good idea and in a sense a statement about postprocessing in portrait :) I think I would have liked it even better if the light would mimic the duality on her body as it does on her face.', '2012-01-06 21:52:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6637322, 990769, 49018, '<td valign="top">Awash with light, nice effect and expressive.</td>', 'Awash with light, nice effect and expressive.', '2012-01-06 21:53:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(6637382, 990065, 76335, '<td valign="top">The eyes strike me as a little overworked in processing. It''s such a wonderful moment, I''m sure it didn''t need any help.</td>', 'The eyes strike me as a little overworked in processing. It''s such a wonderful moment, I''m sure it didn''t need any help.', '2012-01-06 23:16:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(6637383, 990357, 76335, '<td valign="top">Warm. Grin''s a little tight.</td>', 'Warm. Grin''s a little tight.', '2012-01-06 23:16:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(6637384, 990145, 76335, '<td valign="top">Great smile -- he''s engaged. Skin has no texture (?).</td>', 'Great smile -- he''s engaged. Skin has no texture (?).', '2012-01-06 23:17:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6637390, 990698, 76335, '<td valign="top">A little more or less of her left eye would have been better, I think.</td>', 'A little more or less of her left eye would have been better, I think.', '2012-01-06 23:20:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6637393, 990495, 76335, '<td valign="top">Quirky composition. Love the deadpan expression.</td>', 'Quirky composition. Love the deadpan expression.', '2012-01-06 23:21:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(6637398, 990747, 76335, '<td valign="top">Stark and silly -- and just plain wrong. Everything about it is wrong. A nine for you.</td>', 'Stark and silly -- and just plain wrong. Everything about it is wrong. A nine for you.', '2012-01-06 23:22:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(6637401, 990485, 76335, '<td valign="top">Haunting. Good.</td>', 'Haunting. Good.', '2012-01-06 23:24:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6637402, 990498, 76335, '<td valign="top">A little overexposed. I do like the warm smile, the slightly typically boyishly crooked glasses...</td>', 'A little overexposed. I do like the warm smile, the slightly typically boyishly crooked glasses...', '2012-01-06 23:25:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6637407, 990799, 76335, '<td valign="top">I sense a passing moment of distraction or maybe irritation more than wonder. It has as much to do with the mouth as the eyes, I think. I like it for other reasons though -- just unable to reconcile the image to the title.</td>', 'I sense a passing moment of distraction or maybe irritation more than wonder. It has as much to do with the mouth as the eyes, I think. I like it for other reasons though -- just unable to reconcile the image to the title.', '2012-01-06 23:27:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(6637412, 990470, 76335, '<td valign="top">Love the no-nonsense mien, piercing eyes...</td>', 'Love the no-nonsense mien, piercing eyes...', '2012-01-06 23:30:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6637415, 990775, 76335, '<td valign="top">Hard to resist that light, ain''t it? I''ve been known to drag my kids, unannounced, into the backyard at such times. Really nice. I like the low point of view too.</td>', 'Hard to resist that light, ain''t it? I''ve been known to drag my kids, unannounced, into the backyard at such times. Really nice. I like the low point of view too.', '2012-01-06 23:31:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(6637468, 990784, 30364, '<td valign="top">Now this is (intentionally) very clever.  The uncertainty, contradiction and innocence of the age is perfectly represented in your sympathetic treatment.  Your picture is a fine example of when and why convention can be profitably ditched.  It''s in my top three picks, and damned with the faint praise of the Order of the Thumb.  Thank you. <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=800078" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Now this is (intentionally) very clever.  The uncertainty, contradiction and innocence of the age is perfectly represented in your sympathetic treatment.  Your picture is a fine example of when and why convention can be profitably ditched.  It''s in my top three picks, and damned with the faint praise of the Order of the Thumb.  Thank you. ', '2012-01-07 02:17:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(6637477, 990773, 30364, '<td valign="top">This is simply terrific!  It''s always a pleasure to look at photographs that explore the edges of reason, because they are so loaded with possibilities.  Here I see a Confessional where the sinner is provided with adequate sinning opportunity, in order to make the visit a success for everyone involved.  A very sensible approach to both sin and salvation <i>(''As I intend to prosper and repent, so thrive I in my dangerous affairs'')</i>, as well as, of course, to secrets.  It''s in  my top three picks and certainly weird enough to wear an Order of the Thumb.  <i>Gratis tibi ago</i>.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=800078" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg"/></a></td>', 'This is simply terrific!  It''s always a pleasure to look at photographs that explore the edges of reason, because they are so loaded with possibilities.  Here I see a Confessional where the sinner is provided with adequate sinning opportunity, in order to make the visit a success for everyone involved.  A very sensible approach to both sin and salvation (''As I intend to prosper and repent, so thrive I in my dangerous affairs''), as well as, of course, to secrets.  It''s in  my top three picks and certainly weird enough to wear an Order of the Thumb.  Gratis tibi ago.', '2012-01-07 02:43:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6637479, 989979, 30364, '<td valign="top">I like this.  Many will bleat that it isn''t a portrait, but it is for me.  A picture like this of my late father, for example, would have been a perfect portrait of him.  <br/> <br/>The conventional approach to portraits is of course the close up head shot with the pimped eyes and grotesquely smoothed skin.  Or the gnarly head shot with the grunge processing.  <br/> <br/>The conventional approach to the challenge topic (''classic portrait'' and ''typically captures the face'' blah blah blah) is to be constrained by it, rather than liberated by it.<br/> <br/>You''ll be getting blasted for your audacity, just as did <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=146162" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">this fellow traveler.</a> <br/> <br/>Convention and blind obedience suck, don''t they?  Why go along, just to produce something two-dimensional and instantly forgettable?  So BRAVO you, and please accept my top pick, a 10, and an Order of the Thumb.   <br/>Thank you.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=800078" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg"/></a></td>', 'I like this.  Many will bleat that it isn''t a portrait, but it is for me.  A picture like this of my late father, for example, would have been a perfect portrait of him.   The conventional approach to portraits is of course the close up head shot with the pimped eyes and grotesquely smoothed skin.  Or the gnarly head shot with the grunge processing.   The conventional approach to the challenge topic (''classic portrait'' and ''typically captures the face'' blah blah blah) is to be constrained by it, rather than liberated by it. You''ll be getting blasted for your audacity, just as did this fellow traveler.  Convention and blind obedience suck, don''t they?  Why go along, just to produce something two-dimensional and instantly forgettable?  So BRAVO you, and please accept my top pick, a 10, and an Order of the Thumb.   Thank you.', '2012-01-07 02:44:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(6637540, 990504, 109227, '<td valign="top">I think this is a beautiful portrait; I especially like the softness from the glass and the light.  However, my eye keeps jumping to the white line on the side which is very distracting. (voted earlier)</td>', 'I think this is a beautiful portrait; I especially like the softness from the glass and the light.  However, my eye keeps jumping to the white line on the side which is very distracting. (voted earlier)', '2012-01-07 08:26:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(6637542, 989987, 109227, '<td valign="top">I like that this is not overprocessed.  Precious. (voted earlier)</td>', 'I like that this is not overprocessed.  Precious. (voted earlier)', '2012-01-07 08:27:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(6637543, 989904, 109227, '<td valign="top">I like the natural look here, not over processed.  The crop is a little tight, but a nice portrait none-the-less.  (voted earlier)</td>', 'I like the natural look here, not over processed.  The crop is a little tight, but a nice portrait none-the-less.  (voted earlier)', '2012-01-07 08:29:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6637548, 990714, 109227, '<td valign="top">I like this natural expressions.  She looks like she could keep all 13 of them in line, lol.  The reflections in the glasses keep drawing my eye and detract. (voted earlier)</td>', 'I like this natural expressions.  She looks like she could keep all 13 of them in line, lol.  The reflections in the glasses keep drawing my eye and detract. (voted earlier)', '2012-01-07 08:34:31.000000', NULL, 1);
