(6644170, 990077, 61778, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Nusbaum:</b></div><hr/><i> I really like this portrait, but I''m a fan of dark moody images. I''m curious why you cropped so there is so much dark space behind the subject rather than in front of him? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I was trying to portray the idea that the subject had used everything he had to get to the light, but only just. The extra dark space behind the subject supported that.</td>', 'Originally posted by Nusbaum: I really like this portrait, but I''m a fan of dark moody images. I''m curious why you cropped so there is so much dark space behind the subject rather than in front of him?   I was trying to portray the idea that the subject had used everything he had to get to the light, but only just. The extra dark space behind the subject supported that.', '2012-01-13 10:12:17.000000', NULL, 0),
